    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1259">

                <pb facs="1229" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2357</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-18T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 18, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 19, 3.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3642. My 3627. Rubber gloves are used in work on civil and military prisoners.
                    Wounded prisoners here have been splendidly treated. It would be a sad matter if
                    Germans had to cease care of wounded in order to save gloves for their own
                    people. This matter is urgent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
